<h4>Vowel Length Confusion</h4>
<p>Thai distinguishes meaning by vowel length; English does not. This leads to consistent mergers:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>/ɪ/ vs /iː/:</strong> "Sit" and "seat" sound identical.</li>
  <li><strong>/ʊ/ vs /uː/:</strong> "Pull" and "pool" sound identical.</li>
  <li><strong>/æ/ vs /ɑː/:</strong> "Cat" and "cart" sound identical.</li>
</ul>

