<h4>Regional Dialect Influence</h4>
<p>The "Thai English accent" is not monolithic:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Central Thai (Bangkok):</strong> /r/ often becomes /l/ or a tap. Most internationally recognized variant.</li>
  <li><strong>Northern Thai (Chiang Mai):</strong> More initial /h/, longer vowels. Perceived as "softer."</li>
  <li><strong>Isan (Northeastern):</strong> Lao-influenced. /r/ → /h/ or dropped entirely. Distinct tonal patterns carry into English.</li>
  <li><strong>Southern Thai:</strong> Shorter vowels, more glottal stops. Sounds sharper or more clipped.</li>
</ul>

