<h2>Conclusion: Malfunction Is Not Always Accident</h2>
<p>A broken lift can be poor maintenance. It can also be ambient coercion. The difference lives in response, transparency, and respect for those impacted.</p>
<p>Fair infrastructure is predictable, communicative, accountable, and restorative. Coercive infrastructure is erratic, silent, unaccountable, and punishing. Naming the difference doesn't just get elevators fixed faster — it restores agency to those told their discomfort is imaginary.</p>

